    P13 keep the running sums when recomputed rates are bitwise unchanged
    
    simulate-cached resumes its running sums at the first dependent rate whose
    recomputed value differs bitwise, and keeps the previous total when none
    does, for example for saturated, gated or catalyst-only dependencies.
    Covered by the partial-resumption test against Direct.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Sh6qGxYYnoycTZX4JQ64tG

